# Code owners — GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull
# request touches. One maintainer, so the rules are short; they exist so that
# review is requested automatically rather than remembered, and so that the
# paths where a mistake is expensive are visible in one place.
#
# The last matching rule wins, so the specific ones come after the catch-all.

